    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7d00e372_dca6084e",
        "filename": "infra/bots/task_drivers/bazel_test_benchmark/bazel_test_benchmark.go",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 149,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-19T21:44:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003eIs jobs relevant since we aren\u0027t using RBE?\n\nThis is used for compilation on RBE, assuming the passed in config is `linux_rbe` or similar. The number of jobs was copied from other Bazel task drivers.\n\n\u003eOr do we use RBE for compilation still?\n\nGood point. We can use RBE for compilation and run the compiled test locally (e.g. on a Skolo Linux machine) by passing `--strategy\u003dTestRunner\u003dlocal`. \n\nI added `--strategy\u003dTestRunner\u003dlocal` to this task driver under the assumption that we will always want to run benchmarks on bare-metal machines rather than on GCE VMs. This also implies the task driver must run on a bare-metal machine, so I\u0027ve updated my sample CI task to run on a Skolo Linux machine.\n\nAs an alternative to the `--strategy` Bazel flag, I tried tagging the test with `no-remote`, but somehow it still gets executed on RBE.",
      "parentUuid": "28d1ab11_b5e226c1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 149,
        "startChar": 5,
        "endLine": 149,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "38c0a3ec33f0ccc454056723417fe5f2c8f1a11a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
